# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:5 lint/nursery/noChainedComparison ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This compares the result of another comparison with a value.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if ((a === b as boolean) === c) {}
      │     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ if ((a < b)! < c) {}
    4 │ 
  
  i This comparison runs first and produces true or false.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if ((a === b as boolean) === c) {}
      │      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ if ((a < b)! < c) {}
    4 │ 
  
  i This value is then compared with that true or false, not with the values of the first comparison.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if ((a === b as boolean) === c) {}
      │                              ^
    3 │ if ((a < b)! < c) {}
    4 │ 
  
  i For example, 2 === 2 === 2 is false, because 2 === 2 is true, and true === 2 is false.
  
  i To compare each pair of values, join separate comparisons with &&, as in a === b && b === c.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

